\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A1.1}{\ignorespaces Forms of membrane transport and the influence of the membrane. (A) Passive transport moves solutes down their concentration or electrochemical gradient by simple diffusion, channels, or passive carriers. Active transport moves solutes against a gradient and requires metabolic energy. (B) The electrochemical gradient combines the concentration gradient and membrane potential; the electrical and chemical components may reinforce or oppose one another.\FN@sf@gobble@optonly }}{73}{figure.caption.149}%
